Subject: Fuses a strict compare against a just-loaded undefined

What this does
  Fuses a strict compare against a just-loaded undefined.

Why we need it
  But the load the compare immediately reads still dispatches separately.

What it adds
  `regvm_fuse_branches`, when fusing a strict-compare binary with its branch, looks one instruction further back; if that instruction is a `ROP_load_undefined` whose register has no other reader and is one of the compare's two operands, the branch is rewritten to carry a new pseudo sub-op (`REG_BIN_IS_UNDEF` / `REG_BIN_IS_NOT_UNDEF`) and both the load and the compare are dropped; the tag test rides the existing compare-and-branch handlers (the threaded `T_DEF_CMP_BRANCH` and both monolith `REGVM_CMP_BRANCH` macros) and `regvm_cmp_opcode` returns -1 for the new sub-ops so the narrow form is kept.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  Yes. The register blobs are regenerated in 9999. `BC_VERSION` is unchanged.
